[44.326659, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[44.858849, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mif [ -d /proc/5168 ]; then echo 5168 > /app/pypiserver.pid; echo \"server pid 5168 alive\"; else echo \"pid gone\"; fi; cat /app/pypiserver.pid 2>/dev/null; curl -s -o /dev/null -w 'index status: %{http_code}\\n' http://localhost:8080/simple/vectorops/\r\nserver pid 5168 alive\r\n5168\r\nindex status: 200\r\n"]
[45.885754, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[47.46489, "o", "Done. The package is built and a local PyPI server is running on port 8080.\r\n\r\n## What was created\r\n\r\n```\r\n/app/\r\n├── pyproject.toml            # name=vectorops, version=0.1.0\r\n├── README.md\r\n├── vectorops/\r\n│   └── __init__.py           # defines dotproduct and __version__\r\n├── dist/\r\n│   ├── vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\r\n│   └── vectorops-0.1.0.tar.gz\r\n├── pypiserver.log\r\n├── pypiserver.pid\r\n└── start_pypi_server.sh      # rebuild + restart helper\r\n```\r\n\r\n`vectorops/__init__.py` exposes `dotproduct` at the package root, so `from vectorops import dotproduct` works.\r\n\r\n## Verified installation\r\n\r\nRun in a clean virtualenv (from outside `/app`, to ensure the installed copy is used):\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput confirmed:\r\n\r\n```\r\nLooking in indexes: http://localhost:8080/simple\r\nCollecting vectorops==0.1.0\r\n  Downloading http://localhost:8080/packages/vectorops-0.1.0-py3-non"]
[47.46493, "o", "e-any.whl (1.6 kB)\r\nSuccessfully installed vectorops-0.1.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd the required behavior:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom vectorops import dotproduct\r\nassert 1 == dotproduct([1, 1], [0, 1])\r\n```\r\n\r\nPassed, with installed module at `.../site-packages/vectorops/__init__.py`.\r\n\r\n## Server details\r\n\r\n- Simple index: `http://localhost:8080/simple`\r\n- Package page: `http://localhost:8080/simple/vectorops/` (HTTP 200)\r\n- Running via `pypiserver` (PID 5168), serving `/app/dist`\r\n- To rebuild and restart: `./start_pypi_server.sh`\r\n"]
